;; EXPECT: check-failed
;; MESSAGE: disequality is inconclusive
;; A lazy check that used to never return. Each rule round grows the graph about 8x
;; (17, 42, 430, 3774, 29597 nodes: ACI completion folds C back into Min monomials, each a
;; new :flatten match). The node budget counted only nodes minted inside one completion
;; rebuild, never the rule rounds, and one completion round over ~19,000 rules and ~22,000
;; targets ran for minutes while minting almost nothing. The decision now charges every node
;; minted since it opened and bounds each completion round's work (design 06 §13), so the
;; check-neq reports the budget stop as inconclusive within seconds
;; (`lazy_budget_check_returns_promptly` in egg_tests.rs).
(sort E)
(function A () E) (function B () E) (function C () E) (function D () E)
(function Min (E) E :assoc-comm-idem)
(function T (E E) E)
(rewrite (Min x y (C) ..r) (Min (T x y) ..r) :flatten)
(let i (Min (A) (B) (C) (D)))
(set-option :check-completion on)
(check-neq (A) (B))
